\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Schematic comparison of the winding-group spatial arrangements discussed in the text, drawn as star-connected coil groups (each leg a winding phase, small dot the group's local neutral point) inside the stator bore, with the shaft centerline marked for physical context (small grey disk): (a)~approximately aligned groups -- at every one of three representative slots around the bore, group~1 (inner layer) and group~2 (outer layer) occupy the same angular position at different radial depth; (b)~deliberately spatially shifted groups -- both groups sit at the same radial layer, but group~2 is displaced from group~1 by a fixed angle $\Delta \theta =60^\circ $ at every slot, so the six coil clusters interleave evenly around the bore; and (c)~physically segmented stator modules -- the same bore split by four mechanical/magnetic boundaries (dashed radial lines) into four modules that alternate between group~1 and group~2, so each group occupies two diametrically opposite, physically separate segments rather than a single contiguous arc. The arrangement affects mutual coupling, MMF harmonics, and the additional current subspaces available to the controller.}}{6}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:winding_options}{{6}{6}{}{figure.6}{}}
