\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces Nonlinear simulation of SPB dc-link voltage-sharing dynamics for $N=3$ cells, integrating the exact constant-power-load model of \cite  {Nikouie2017Stability} (not its linearization) from the same initial per-cell voltage deviations ($+8\%$, $-5\%$, $+2\%$ of $v^\star $) with and without their proportional balancing controller. Without balancing (left), the open-loop instability proven in \cite  {Nikouie2017Stability} drives Cell~2's voltage toward collapse within about 2~ms while Cells~1 and~3 compensate; with balancing (right, same initial conditions, same time axis), all three cells converge back toward $v^\star $ on a comparable timescale. This is a computed simulation result using real experimental circuit parameters from the cited reference, not measured hardware data.}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
