\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {13}{\ignorespaces Control block diagram for a representative cell $k$ under each of the three SPB dc-link balancing approaches of Table~\ref {fig:spb_balancing_taxonomy}. All three share the same forward path -- a common current-control loop sets $v_d^\star ,v_q^\star $ for every cell, and a summing junction ahead of the $dq{\to }\alpha \beta $/PWM stage admits a per-cell correction $\Delta v_{d,k},\Delta v_{q,k}$ -- following the structure used for the ``controller alternative I'' simulation of Fig.~\ref {fig:spb_balancing_dynamics} \cite  {Nikouie2017Stability}. (a)~Centralized: one controller senses every cell's $V_{\mathrm  {dc},k}$ and computes $v_{\mathrm  {ref}}=\tfrac  1N\DOTSB \sum@ \slimits@ _kV_{\mathrm  {dc},k}$ \cite  {Nikouie2015Stability,Nikouie2017Stability}. (b)~CDR: the balancing block is absent entirely ($\Delta v_{d,k}=\Delta v_{q,k}=0$); all cells receive the same open-loop command and balancing relies on the natural coupled converter--machine dynamics \cite  {Mocevic2023CDR}. (c)~Distributed: each cell computes its own local $v_{\mathrm  {ref}}$ from its own voltage and neighbour-only measurements exchanged with Cell~$k{-}1$ and Cell~$k{+}1$, with no central node \cite  {Verkroost2024VoltageBalance}.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:balancing_control_diagrams}{{13}{13}{}{figure.13}{}}
\newlabel{eq:semiconductor_rating}{{18}{13}{}{equation.18}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {14}{\ignorespaces Cell-count scaling for a 1200-V dc link: nominal cell voltage $V_{\mathrm  {cell,nom}}=V_{\mathrm  {dc}}/N$ (solid markers, left log axis) and active-switch count $6N$ (dashed markers, right linear axis) versus cell count $N$; every marker is labeled directly with its exact value ($N=1$: 1200~V, 6; $N=2$: 600~V, 12; $N=3$: 400~V, 18; $N=4$: 300~V, 24; $N=5$: 240~V, 30; $N=8$: 150~V, 48; $N=10$: 120~V, 60; $N=15$: 80~V, 90). Increasing $N$ opens progressively lower commercial semiconductor voltage classes (e.g., 1700--2000-V SiC at $N=1$, 650-V GaN/SiC at $N=3$, 100-V GaN/MOSFET class at $N=15$) while the active-switch count grows linearly as $6N$.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cell_count_scaling}{{14}{13}{}{figure.14}{}}
